ass="node-icon-bg" x="279" y="820" width="26" height="26" rx="7"/><path class="node-icon" transform="translate(283 824) scale(0.75)" d="M5 6.500c0-1.400 3.100-2.500 7-2.500s7 1.100 7 2.500-3.100 2.500-7 2.500-7-1.100-7-2.500z M5 6.500v11c0 1.400 3.100 2.500 7 2.500s7-1.100 7-2.500v-11 M5 12c0 1.400 3.100 2.500 7 2.500s7-1.100 7-2.500"/><text class="node-title" x="319" y="829" font-size="13" text-anchor="start">Agent store</text><text class="node-tech" x="319" y="846" font-size="11" text-anchor="start">Agent definitions + version history</text></g><g class="node" style="--k:var(--c3)"><rect class="node-box" x="529" y="794" width="236" height="78" rx="10"/><rect class="node-icon-bg" x="541" y="820" width="26" height="26" rx="7"/><path class="node-icon" transform="translate(545 824) scale(0.75)" d="M5 6.500c0-1.400 3.100-2.500 7-2.500s7 1.100 7 2.500-3.100 2.500-7 2.500-7-1.100-7-2.500z M5 6.500v11c0 1.400 3.100 2.500 7 2.500s7-1.100 7-2.500v-11 M5 12c0 1.400 3.100 2.500 7 2.500s7-1.100 7-2.500"/><text class="node-title" x="581" y="822" font-size="13" text-anchor="start">Run log</text><text class="node-tech" x="581" y="839" font-size="11" text-anchor="start">Inputs, outputs, ratings, accepted</text><text class="node-tech" x="581" y="853" font-size="11" text-anchor="start">improvements</text></g><g class="node mock" style="--k:var(--muted)"><rect class="node-box" x="791" y="794" width="236" height="78" rx="10"/><rect class="node-icon-bg" x="803" y="820" width="26" height="26" rx="7"/><path class="node-icon" transform="translate(807 824) scale(0.75)" d="M4 20v-12l5-3v15 M9 20v-9h11v9z M12.500 14h1.500 M16 14h1.500 M12.500 17h1.500 M16 17h1.500 M3 20h18"/><text class="node-title" x="843" y="829" font-size="13" text-anchor="start">Company knowledge base</text><text class="node-tech" x="843" y="846" font-size="11" text-anchor="start">SharePoint / intranet (mocked)</text><rect class="tag-state" x="986.2" y="787" width="30.8" height="14" rx="7"/><text class="tag-state-text" x="1001.6" y="797.2" font-size="8.5" text-anchor="middle">MOCK</text></g></svg></div><div class="legend"><span class="key kind" style="--k:var(--muted)"><i></i>People</span><span class="key kind" style="--k:var(--c0)"><i></i>Interface</span><span class="key kind" style="--k:var(--c1)"><i></i>Agent</span><span class="key kind" style="--k:var(--c4)"><i></i>Model</span><span class="key kind" style="--k:var(--c2)"><i></i>Tool or API</span><span class="key kind" style="--k:var(--c3)"><i></i>Data</span><span class="key kind" style="--k:var(--muted)"><i></i>Existing system</span><span class="key ibm"><i>IBM</i>IBM technology</span><span class="key dashed"><i></i>Planned or mocked, not built yet</span></div></figure><p class="fine">Dashed nodes are mocked in the proof of concept with synthetic data and invented policy docs. Interfaces are the real ones — the mock is swapped for the live system in the pilot.</p><div class="split wide"><div class="callout"><h4>IBM technology in this solution</h4><ul><li><b>Agent runner</b> — Executes the agent with grounded instructions on each run</li><li><b>Improvement engine</b> — Turns a rating + comment into a concrete, actionable prompt edit suggestion</li><li><b>Bob IDE</b> — Build environment: agent definitions, tools, tests and the task session report for judges</li></ul></div><div class="decisions"><div class="decision"><h4>Grounding, not fine-tuning</h4><p>Company knowledge is passed as context on each run. No model is fine-tuned, so the PoC runs without data export approval and the knowledge stays current without retraining.</p></div><div class="decision"><h4>Improvement is a suggestion, not an automatic rewrite</h4><p>The agent never updates its own instructions without the user&#x27;s explicit acceptance. This keeps a person in the loop and avoids drift.</p></div><div class="decision"><h4>Mocks behind real interfaces</h4><p>The PoC runs on synthetic data. The policy store, email connector and CRM expose the same API the real systems would, so the mock is replaced by an adapter in the pilot without changing the agent.</p></div><div class="decision"><h4>Built entirely in Bob</h4><p>The task session report in Bob IDE is part of the submission. Building outside Bob loses that evidence for the judges.</p></div></div></div></div></section><section id="impact"><div class="wrap"><header class="sec-head"><div class="kicker"><b>04</b>Impact</div><h2>Each run takes <strong>minutes instead of half an hour</strong>. The agent remembers what good looks like.</h2><p class="lead">The primary metric is time-to-acceptable-output per recurring task. The secondary metric is rating trajectory: do accepted improvements lead to higher ratings on the next run?</p></header><div class="metrics"><div class="metric"><div class="metric-name">Time to acceptable output<span class="basis assumption" title="Before: estimated from 3 runs × 5 min iteration + 25 min total. After: target for the PoC. Pilot will measure."><i></i>Assumption</span></div><div class="bars"><div class="bar-row"><span class="bar-tag">Before</span><div class="bar-track"><div class="bar before" style="width:100%"></div></div><span class="bar-value">40 <span class="unit">min per run</span></span></div><div class="bar-row"><span class="bar-tag">After</span><div class="bar-track"><div class="bar after" style="width:15%"></div></div><span class="bar-value"><b>6</b> <span class="unit">min per run</span></span></div></div><div class="delta big good">7× less</div></div><div class="metric"><div class="metric-name">Prompt setup time at session start<span class="basis assumption" title="Before: employee rewrites prompt from memory. After: agent retains instructions between sessions."><i></i>Assumption</span></div><div class="bars"><div class="bar-row"><span class="bar-tag">Before</span><div class="bar-track"><div class="bar before" style="width:100%"></div></div><span class="bar-value">8 <span class="unit">min</span></span></div><div class="bar-row"><span class="bar-tag">After</span><div class="bar-track"><div class="bar after" style="width:12.5%"></div></div><span class="bar-value"><b>1</b> <span class="unit">min</span></span></div></div><div class="delta big good">8× less</div></div><div class="metric"><div class="metric-name">Agent rating after 5 runs<span class="basis assumption" title="Target: accepted improvements measurably raise the average rating over 5 runs. Pilot will measure."><i></i>Assumption</span></div><div class="bars"><div class="bar-row"><span class="bar-tag">Before</span><div class="bar-track"><div class="bar before" style="width:50%"></div></div><span class="bar-value">2 <span class="unit">out of 5</span></span></div><div class="bar-row"><span class="bar-tag">After</span><div class="bar-track"><div class="bar after" style="width:100%"></div></div><span class="bar-value"><b>4</b> <span class="unit">out of 5</span></span></div></div><div class="delta big good">×2</div></div><div class="metric"><div class="metric-name">Runs before first acceptable output<span class="basis assumption" title="Pilot measurement: compare with and without improvement loop active."><i></i>Assumption</span></div><div class="bars"><div class="bar-row"><span class="bar-tag">Before</span><div class="bar-track"><div class="bar before" style="width:100%"></div></div><span class="bar-value">3 <span class="unit">runs</span></span></div><div class="bar-row"><span class="bar-tag">After</span><div class="bar-track"><div class="bar after" style="width:33.3%"></div></div><span class="bar-value"><b>1</b> <span class="unit">runs</span></span></div></div><div class="delta big good">−67%</div></div></div><figure class="card"><figcaption>Indicative yearly value per 100 knowledge workers</figcaption><svg class="diagram waterfall" viewBox="0 0 720 310" role="img" aria-label="Indicative yearly value per 100 knowledge workers" direction="ltr" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><line class="axis" x1="8" x2="712" y1="260" y2="260"/><rect class="wf pos